`.length` on a map is the map's size on every target.

The checker typed `.length` as int on a list or a string only, so on a map it
was an unchecked `dyn` select and each backend spelled a field read: JavaScript
`m.length`, undefined on a `Map`, and Kotlin `m.length`, which does not compile.
Go's `len(m)` was right by accident. `cmd/sngl/testdata/map_length_runs.txt`
executes it.

deny out/none/html/index.html `stock\.length` -- a JS Map has no length; its count is size
deny out/kotlin/android/app/src/main/java/test/sngl/app/MainScreen.kt `stock\.length` -- a Kotlin Map has no length; its count is size
-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
    none {
        html
    }
    kotlin {
        android
    }
}

ui.window {
    var stock map<string, int> = {"a"=1}

    ui.text(value="{stock.length}")
}
